- The template claims to be "VOD academy streaming video assets" but there is zero AWS Elemental MediaConvert pipeline defined. Raw MP4 uploads to S3 are not production-ready for global multi-bitrate streaming. You need adaptive bitrate (ABR) encoding to HLS/DASH with multiple renditions (240p/480p/720p/1080p) so Smart TVs in countries with poor connectivity (parts of Poland, Brazil) auto-adapt:

```yaml
MediaConvertRole:
  Type: 'AWS::IAM::Role'
  Properties:
    RoleName: !Sub 'FixyachipsMediaConvertRole-${AWS::StackName}'
    AssumeRolePolicyDocument:
      Version: '2012-10-17'
      Statement:
        - Effect: Allow
          Principal:
            Service: mediaconvert.amazonaws.com
          Action: 'sts:AssumeRole'
    Policies:
      - PolicyName: MediaConvertS3Access
        PolicyDocument:
          Version: '2012-10-17'
          Statement:
            - Effect: Allow
              Action:
                - 's3:GetObject'
                - 's3:PutObject'
              Resource:
                - !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}/raw-uploads/*'
                - !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}/vod/*'
                - !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}/hls/*'
                - !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}/dash/*'

VideoProcessingTrigger:
  Type: 'AWS::Lambda::Function'
  Properties:
    FunctionName: !Sub 'FixyachipsVideoProcessor-${AWS::StackName}'
    Handler: index.lambda_handler
    Runtime: python3.12
    Role: !GetAtt FixyachipsMasterRole.Arn
    MemorySize: 512
    Timeout: 60
    Environment:
      Variables:
        MEDIACONVERT_ENDPOINT: ''    # Populate via custom resource or SSM
        MEDIACONVERT_ROLE_ARN: !GetAtt MediaConvertRole.Arn
