**CRITICAL ERROR — Accept-Language Header Forwarding Will Destroy Cache Hit Ratio**

- **Do NOT forward `Accept-Language` headers in the Origin Request Policy for VOD content.** This is the most common mistake in multi-lingual CloudFront architectures. If Accept-Language is included in the cache key, every unique language header variant creates a separate cache entry. A German user on Chrome sends `de-DE,de;q=0.9,en;q=0.8` while a German user on Firefox sends `de,en-US;q=0.7` — these are two different cache keys for the same German `/de/index.html` page, obliterating your cache hit ratio.

- **The correct architecture is path-based routing only**: `/es/*`, `/de/*`, `/fr/*` etc. Content is stored in S3 under language-prefixed paths. CloudFront caches by path. No header forwarding needed. The corrected function above implements this.

