- **FINOPS SAVINGS — Lambda MemorySize Not Set: Defaults to 128MB Cold Start Tax**

`SignupWorker` has no `MemorySize`. AWS defaults to 128MB. A Python 3.12 function cold-starting with boto3, DynamoDB, and two SES calls at 128MB runs 800ms–1.4s. At 256MB the same function runs in ~300ms. Lambda bills on GB-seconds — 256MB at 300ms costs the same or less than 128MB at 800ms, and your students get a faster signup confirmation.

```yaml
SignupWorker:
  Type: 'AWS::Lambda::Function'
  Properties:
    FunctionName: !Sub 'FixyachipsSignupWorker-${AWS::StackName}'
    Handler: index.lambda_handler
    Runtime: python3.12
    Role: !GetAtt FixyachipsMasterRole.Arn
    Timeout: 15                          # REDUCED from 30: SES+DynamoDB never needs 30s
    MemorySize: 256                      # ADDED: eliminates cold-start penalty
    ReservedConcurrentExecutions: 100    # ADDED: hard cap prevents runaway cost during bot surge
    DeadLetterConfig:
      TargetArn: !GetAtt SignupWorkerDLQ.Arn   # ADDED: see DLQ resource below
    Environment:
