- **CRITICAL ERROR — Do NOT Forward Accept-Language Header in Cache Key**

This is the most common cache-destruction mistake in multi-lingual CloudFront deployments. If `Accept-Language` is forwarded in the cache key, Chrome on Windows sends `de-DE,de;q=0.9,en;q=0.8` while Firefox sends `de,en-US;q=0.7,en;q=0.3`. These are two different cache keys for the identical `/de/index.html` page. Your global cache hit ratio collapses to near zero and every request pays Origin Shield charges.

**The correct architecture is path-based routing exclusively.** Content stored at `/de/`, `/es/`, `/fr/` in S3. CloudFront caches by path. Zero header forwarding. The CloudFront Function transparently prepends the language prefix. This is already implemented in the corrected function above.

